<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends flat against dollar.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends flat against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka closed flat at 43.7500/7600 to the dollar in interbank trading in an active session on Monday, dealers said. The taka was quoted weaker at 43.7900/8000 per dollar in early trade but recovered later amid tight liquidity in the local currency market.</p>
<p>The call money was traded in a wide range between eight to 11 percent against a previous 11-12 percent.</p>
<p>- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
